e the Word out there, you know, to bless the World. So if you are visiting with us this morning, that''s what we are going to be doing a lot. We''re going to be reflecting a lot, and using the Word of God as a mirror, you know, just to see, you know, one or two things that we can do differently, especially around the topic of being grateful, you know, to the Lord. Um, that Bible passage that we read, you know, uh, Psalm 103, uh, says, Bless the Lord, O my soul, and forget not all His benefits. It says, forget not all His benefits. You see, one of the greatest dangers that we have as Christians is not… Uh, yes, we suffer persecution, we know, you know, there''s a lot going on around us, you know, uh, we suffer opposition, but one important, you know, dangers that we can easily get into as Christians is our forgetfulness. We can easily forget a lot, a lot, a lot, a lot of things. And one of those things that we can easily forget is all around how we should be thankful in various ways, in various blessings that we have received. A lot of us will remember our problems. You know, we will remember it more than the provisions that we have received from the Lord. We focus on that particular thing that we''ve been asking God for, and we forget about everything that the Lord has surrounded us with. You know what the Bible says? It continuously, daily loads us with blessings. And we just don''t think about the last minute. We just don''t think about the last hour. We just continue to focus on that particular problem. Yes, there are trials. you know, uh… more than God''s triumphs, and their disappointment more than God''s deliverances. That''s what our… most of us focus on. You know, a lot of those trials, a lot of, you know, those disappointments, but we forget about the victories, about the deliverances that we have received. You see, gratitude, when we are thankful, is not just about us saying, thank you, Lord. But you see, it is our lifestyle. It should be our lifestyle. It should be an acknowledgement of God''s goodness in every season. You know, David is a man that was in danger all the time. You know, David was in danger, he was surrounded by danger, everywhere he goes, he doesn''t even know where the danger is coming from, he was continuously hiding. And you know what he says? He says, bless the Lord, despite all this, oh my soul, and forget not all his benefits. Despite the dangers, despite all the, you know, things that he was running away from that were pursuing him, but at the same time, he continues to focus on the blessings of the Lord. And today, what I will try to encourage us to do, and I''m hoping that we''ll be able to achieve at the end of this message, is to be able to say, Lord, I will never be ungrateful to you. How great their God is. Every single way, they enjoy God''s goodness. Every single turn, they enjoy God''s goodness. But you know what happens the next minute? They tend to forget. how great their God was. The same God that parted the Red Sea, you know, that parted the Red Sea, and was able to hold water for them, they believe that the same God cannot provide water for them. They believe the same God cannot provide water for them, and they complain about lack of water. God provided manna. Daily. And on… and at the same time, the children of Israel were still complaining about food. Okay, God guide them. Make sure they went through their journey with cloud and fire. And yet, they forget how great this God is. And they decided to, you know what, to have another God. The same God that provided every single. benefit, took them from where they were in slavery to that Promised Land, and promised them good things that''s going to come. And along the way, continues to show them how great He is. And you know what? They continuously forget. All these blessings. Deuteronomy 8-11 says that, beware that you do not forget the Lord your God. And I want us to remember this morning that. There are many things that God has done for us, and you know what? We have stopped thanking Him for those things. The gift of life is one of those. The fact that we have life and we are assisting this morning is not by our own means. our health that we enjoy, the good health that we enjoy. Yes, there may be one or two things here and there, but at the same time, God is still on the throne. It could be worse. It''s on, but I put it to my ear. I''ll hear it clearly. That''s for sure. Our family that God has blessed us with, the salvation that we receive, the protection that we receive, the daily provisions that He continues to give unto us. The open doors that He has given unto us. The divine faithfuls that we have received, as someone that I can say. His life is full of the grace of God. I can tell you… I can begin to tell you how great has been good to this young man standing in front of you this morning. It is God''s grace. If you know where I was, you know, maybe 40 years ago… no, I''m giving something away now. If you know where God has brought me from in the last 40 years, 30 years, you will know why someone like me is supposed to be thanking God every single minute. It is important that, you know, we make it a habit to always count our blessings. Before we count our bodies. Let''s remember it''s important for us to count our blessings before we start to count our burdens. But unfortunately for us, many Christians, most of our prayers are requests, and a few are just thanksgiving. Everything is all about, God, I want this, I want this, I want this. And we forget to even thank Him. For the fact that we''re even able to ask him. The second point I want us, I want us to, you know, I want us to talk about this morning is that gratitude recognizes that everything comes from God. If you are thanking God, you are thanking God because you believe. That He has given you those things in the first instance. James 1.17 says that every good gift and every perfect gift is from above. Every good and perfect gift is from above. Whatever you possess is by God''s grace. Our abilities to even be able to do one or two things that we''re able to do is from God. The achievement that we have in various ways, in various endeavors, in the successes that we have, they are all from God. Opportunities that we have are from God. 1 Corinthians 4.7 says that, for who makes you different from anyone else? What do you have that you did not receive? And if you did, if you did receive it, why do you boast as though you did not? That is God speaking to us this morning. that everything that we have is from Him. What do you have that you did not receive? There is nothing that we''ve been able to achieve by our own ability. Everything that we have is from God. What do you have that you did not receive? And you know what? Most… for most of us, you know, in small… in small way, in big thing, the pride in us, we say that, I achieved this. But what is very important is that the gratitude in us should be able to say that God enabled me to achieve this. The more successful our people, you know, especially most of us become, the easier it is to forget the source of our blessings. And that''s why maybe sometimes people will say that it''s maybe harder for a rich man to thank God. Because… It''s going it all. You know, but what is very important for us as Christians is whether we have it small, whether we have it big, whether we have it even bigger, let us be able to say that God enabled me. It is not about I, I, I, I. And a good example for us in the Bible is King Nebuchadnezzar. You know, the king of Babylon. He had it all. You know, and one day he woke up, he said, oh, is this not the great Babylon that I have built? I have built. He saw it, you know, he''s got it all, he could see it. Different directions that he looked, and he was able to boast, to say that this is all about me. I did this, and you know what happened to him? Pride brought him down. I pray that''s not going to be our portion this morning, in Jesus'' name. Every achievement that we have should become an altar of thanksgiving. We just need to wake up and say, Lord, you gave me this. And thank God for it. If it is something, you know, a landmark, then we should make it, you know, an altar of thanksgiving. Whenever God blesses you. Remember to give Him glory. Give him the praise. Give him the honor. The next point I want us to also look at this morning is that. Our gratitude must continue even during difficult seasons. I know this is a very, very difficult, you know, point for most of us, because, you know, a lot of us, I''m sure we are thinking, you know, um, yes, I want to thank God, but my circumstance is not thanking God. You know, yes, it''s important for me to thank God, but what''s my art is not innate. You know, I look, you know, this is going on, that is going on, you know, look at this, look at that. Yes. But we have to remember. Even the small things that God has answered us for. Many people will thank God when prayers are answered, you know, but you know what? Actually. Mature believers, we thank God. You know, even while they are waiting. So it''s not just in time, you know, that we have received things, it''s also in times of waiting that we need to thank God. And the Bible passage that we read this morning, which is in Habakkuk chapter 3, and I want someone to read that passage to us, you know, once again. Habakkuk chapter 3, verse, um, um, 17. Um, can you, you know, whoever is reading, can you read slowly? And I will ask you to stop at some point. Yes? Yes. Yes? Yes, yes, stop. Is there anything to thank God for there? Everything is negative. You know, the victory, yes, that''s again, the victory is… The fruit trees shall not blossom. Yes, the fruit trees shall not blossom. Stop. Yes. My loss of food is. Now shall thy fruit be in the farm. There''s no food in the house. Yes. The labor of the olive shall fail. The labor of the olive shall fail. So every single thing this person has put into farming, into doing what and doing, bringing food into the yards has failed. Yes? The field shall yield no meat. Even the field is not producing anything. In a book. Yes? The flock shall be cut off. The flock shall be cut off. Even the animals are not even, you know, there. Yes. And there shall be no herb in the stalk. And there shall be no herb in the stalk. Yes. Okay, now go on. Yes, I will rejoice in the Lord. Yes, I will rejoice in the Lord. you know, that''s a good place to thank God. Because the circumstances, you know, everything before that is all negative, there is nothing to thank God for. You know, and some… and believe, you know, maybe this is where some of us are this morning, when we look at our circumstances, when we look at our situations, there is nothing to thank God for. But this Abba Cook is telling us this morning that, yet, we should do what? We should thank the Lord. It is not about our circumstances, it is about the goodness of the Lord, and I''m going to tell you about one or two things about that this morning. That is… maturity in being gratitude to the Lord. Another example is Job. Job lost possessions, he lost his children, he lost his health. He lost every single thing that the Lord has blessed him with. And you know what he said in Job chapter 1, verse 21? He said, the Lord gave, and the Lord has taken away. Blessed be the name of the same Lord. Gratitude during abundance is very, very easy. When we have it all, it''s very, you know, easy for us to thank the Lord, but gratitude during difficulty is actually more powerful. Because it demonstrates our faith in the Lord, because we know that our God is still good, even when our circumstances are not. Romans 8.28 says that all things work together for good to those who do well, who love the Lord. We should never allow our temporary problem to erase our permanent blessings. What we believe is that whatever we are going through, as long as our God is still on the throne, they are going to be what? Temporary. And the blessings of the Lord are going to be permanent. Gratitude. The next point is gratitude opens doors for greater blessings. Now, we have a very, very good example of this in Luke chapter 17, verses 11 to 19. The story of the 10 lepers that Jesus healed. Jesus healed 10 lepers, and you know what happened? Only one of God. Came back to the Lord to say, thank you, Lord. The rest of them, I just, I''m just thinking, what happened to the rest of them? And only one of them, you know, you just forget. These people, you know, they''ve had the disease for all their life. And Jesus healed them just like that. And you know what they did in the next minute? They forgot to even thank the person that healed them. And only one of them, out of 10 people. Came back to thank the Lord. Where are we? Are we the one? Or are we one of those nine? It''s very important for us to think and ponder about questions like this. Because we can easily forget. Where we were five minutes ago. last week, a year ago, even years ago, we should remember, you know, things that the Lord has done concerning each and every one of us, and then we''ll be able to decide whether we want to be one of those nine. I want to be the only one that came back. And you know what Jesus said to the one that came back? He said, where are the others? And because I knew there were 10 of you, only one of you has come back. Where are the other 9? The thankful man. Actually, it wasn''t just yield. You know, what happened to him? He received extra… Blessing. Because you know what? It was made old. So, being thankful, yes, we are open doors for more blessings, so that we can be whole. The others were ill, but they decided to be grateful… decided, you know, uh, others were ill, but the grateful one was made whole. Thankfulness attracts God''s attention. I know what complaining means, it magnifies our problems. Which one are we doing this morning? Are we being thankful and just acknowledging God that despite the circumstances that we have, our God is still on the throne? Because if we begin to focus on, you know, those problems, those problems will continue to do what? To get bigger. And being thankful will always magnify our God. There is request, actually, in Thanksgiving. When we are thanking God, we are also bringing our requests before Him. Because if we look at Philippians 4.6, Philippians 4.6 says that, with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known. unto God. There are different ways that we can interpret that passage. You know, we can continue to thank God, but you know what it says? With thanksgiving, let your requests be known unto God. Because you know what you are doing? You are thanking God for that things, for those things that you are bringing before Him, even before they began to manifest. You know, so when we are thanking God, or when we have requests for God, we shouldn''t just say, God, I want this. We should begin to thank Him. And that will help us to thank Him for the great… for the things that we have received, and also begin to thank Him for the things that we are looking forward in anticipation that He''s going to do. Because as we are bringing those requests before Him, He will always be a good God unto us. And as I said, the Bible tells us that He continuously, daily loads us with blessings. We should continue to pray with thanksgiving, and when gratitude becomes our lifestyle, God entrusts us with even more. And the fifth point that I want us to look at again this morning is the greatest things, the greatest reason we must never be ungrateful for is actually our salvation. We should never be ungrateful. to God for our salvation. Among all the blessings that we receive from God, our salvation is the greatest. Because all the blessings that we are, you know, all those things, good things, wonderful things that God has blessed us, they are temporary. But our salvation is permanent. It is eternal. Romans 5:8 says that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us. We didn''t even do anything to deserve the salvation. We were still sinners, yet Christ died for us. Ephesians 2.8 says that, for by grace are ye saved through faith. We were saved through grace. It''s nothing that we did that made us to deserve that self-sufficient. And are we being thankful for it? Are we being or are we being ungrateful? What did we do to deserve the salvation? Actually, nothing. It is only God''s gifts. We may lose material possessions, we may face difficulties, but you know what? If we believe. in our God, we know that we have every reason to be grateful. Because… The Lord sent His own Son, His only Son, to come and die for our sins, and He went on that cross. With everything. And you know what that cross is, you know, is doing this morning? The same cross is speaking God''s love. It''s speaking God''s mercy. It''s speaking God''s grace. It''s speaking God''s forgiveness. But I will thank Him for it every single day, every single minute. Every day we shoot. Always remember to thank God for Jesus. And just to round it all up, you know, again, I''ll go back to, you know, David. David is a great man. He''s a great man that knew how to thank God. He''s a great man that we can learn a lot from, okay? It''s because he says in Psalm 34 verse 1, he says. I will bless the Lord at all times. His praise shall continually be in my mouth. If you notice, it didn''t say, I''ll praise the Lord sometimes. It didn''t say, I''ll praise the Lord when my circumstances are great. It didn''t say, I''ll praise the Lord when my prayers are answered. It says, I''ll praise the Lord at all times. Today, our focus is on Thanksgiving, you know, especially as we''re celebrating 60, you know, great years of our, you know, of our father, you know, of our, you know, uncle, of our mentor, of our… who else? Brother, you know, and to me. Grandfather. You know, we should be thankful to the Lord, you know, just like our brother is doing this morning. Each and every one of us, it is very important that we are thankful. You know, because… Everything that we have is from above. Even in terms of blessings, in terms of the salvation that we have received through Jesus Christ. And our prayer this morning is that… should be that God will remove every spirit of mourning, complaining, and entitlement from our lives. Because that''s a very important one as well. We are not entitled to anything. We are receiving it by God''s grace. We will always remember His goodness and we will have a heart that remembers His goodness daily. We will remain grateful in seasons of abundance and insecurity. We will always acknowledge His grace. and we will trust Him through difficulties. We will thank Him for salvation, and we will live a life that is full of gratitude unto the Lord. So this morning, as we''ll, you know, round up this word, I just want us to close our eyes and just continue to. thank the Lord and bless Him for everything that He has done. And I want you to just repeat, you know, these words after me. Say, Lord, no matter what happens, no matter where You take me. No matter how much you bless me with, I will never be ungrateful to you. Let us begin to thank the Lord.',
